  "_README": [
    "HAND-AUTHORED. This is the one data file in the project that is not generated.",
    "Irish Lights publishes no structured field for tower shape or paint scheme, so each",
    "entry here was read off that station's own photographs (src/scripts/raw/contact-sheet).",
    "",
    "`evidence` is honest about how each entry was arrived at:",
    "  photo   — a usable elevation of the tower was visible in the station's photographs",
    "  generic — the photographs showed only distant aerials or equipment, so no accurate",
    "            profile could be read. These get a deliberately neutral tower and the UI",
    "            says so. Do NOT invent plausible-looking paint schemes for these: a",
    "            confident-looking wrong tower is worse than an honest generic one.",
    "            Promote to `photo` if better imagery turns up.",
    "",
    "bands are fractions of tower height measured from the base (0 = ground, 1 = gallery).",
    "Keys must match the station `id` in lighthouses.json. Unknown keys are ignored.",
    "Rebuild after editing:  uv run src/scripts/build_dataset.py"
